WEBVTT

00:01:58.663 --> 00:02:00.246
this bias flips.

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:02.121
Let's go back to that football game.

00:02:02.163 --> 00:02:03.663
If a player scores a goal,

00:02:03.704 --> 00:02:07.871
it ultimately has a stronger impact
on your impression of their skills

00:02:07.913 --> 00:02:10.121
than if they miss the net.

00:02:11.538 --> 00:02:15.913
The two sides of the updating story
are ultimately quite consistent.

00:02:16.204 --> 00:02:19.413
Overall, behaviors that are perceived
as being less frequent

00:02:19.454 --> 00:02:22.288
are also the ones people tend 
to weigh more heavily

00:02:22.329 --> 00:02:25.996
when forming and updating impressions,

00:02:26.038 --> 00:02:29.496
highly immoral actions
and highly competent actions.

00:02:29.579 --> 00:02:31.788
So, what is happening
at the level of the brain